      'faq.a2b':"Not strictly, but for the best recommendations, yes. Segue's key and energy matching only ever reads what's already tagged in your Rekordbox library — it doesn't analyze audio itself. Mixed In Key is the standard tool DJs use to tag tracks with accurate Camelot keys and energy ratings, so the more of your library it's covered, the sharper Segue's picks will be.",
      'faq.q3':'Can I move my license to a new Mac?',
      'faq.a3':"Yes. Deactivate it from the old machine under Segue's Help menu, then activate the same key on the new one — no need to contact support for a routine switch.",
